[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2935539391","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#issuecomment-2935539391","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107075","id":2935539391,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u-Ma_","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T14:23:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T14:23:05Z","body":"> I think making `Object::has_method()` virtual should be discussed with the core team\n> \n> Personally, I have kind of mixed feelings about it. This will mean that there are methods that will return `true` for `has_method()` but that won't be included in `get_method_list()`, which isn't currently the case.\n> \n> We already have `JavaClass::get_java_method_list()` to list methods from Java - perhaps we should just add a `JavaClass::has_java_method()` and not mess with `Object`?\n\nI went with that approach for consistency; users expect to use `has_method()` to check for a method's existence, they would expect the same for `JavaClassWrapper` and `JNISingleton` (see the issue referenced in the description). \nI wasn't aware that `get_java_method_list()` was the counterpart for `get_method_list()`, but I would also be in favor of overriding the latter for consistency as well.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2935539391/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2935832176","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#issuecomment-2935832176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107075","id":2935832176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u_T5w","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T15:05:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T15:05:34Z","body":"> I wasn't aware that `get_java_method_list()` was the counterpart for `get_method_list()`, but I would also be in favor of overriding the latter for consistency as well.\r\n\r\nIf we made both `has_method()` and `get_method_list()` virtual, that would allow making those consistent with each other, which would be good. I still feel a little unsure about this, though","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2935832176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2936003651","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#issuecomment-2936003651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107075","id":2936003651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u_9xD","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T15:32:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T15:32:26Z","body":"I think, it's better to support `has_method()` and `get_method_list()` instead of having counterparts. But yeah, I agree that it should be discussed with core.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"