sWrapper` classes within `Object` implementations and explicitly call `has_java_method()` and `get_java_method_list()` from there.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2939836531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2939934996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#issuecomment-2939934996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107075","id":2939934996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vO9kU","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T12:54:37Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T12:54:37Z","body":"> @dsnopek An alternative to making both methods virtual would be to check for `JNISingleton` and `JavaClassWrapper` classes within `Object` implementations and explicitly call `has_java_method()` and `get_java_method_list()` from there.\r\n\r\nThat'd require an `include` from `object.cpp` onto `platform/android/api`.. are dependencies from `core` to `platform` allowed?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2939934996/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940162550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#issuecomment-2940162550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107075","id":2940162550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vP1H2","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T14:01:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T14:01:34Z","body":"> This would introduce a path for `Object` subclasses to define methods that are not registered in `ClassDB`, introducing 'dynamic typing' as a whole new concept to our ecosystem.\r\n\r\nIt's already possible for classes to have \"dynamic methods\" that aren't registered in `ClassDB`, which is used in a couple places, including `JavaClassWrapper` (for Android) and `JavaScriptBridge` (for the web).\r\n\r\nHowever, those methods aren't currently recognized by `has_method()` and `get_method_list()`\r\n\r\n> > @dsnopek An alternative to making both methods virtual would be to check for `JNISingleton` and `JavaClassWrapper` classes within `Object` implementations and explicitly call `has_java_method()` and `get_java_method_list()` from there.\r\n> \r\n> That'd require an `include` from `object.cpp` onto `platform/android/api`.. are dependencies from `core` to `platform` allowed?\r\n\r\nI think I probably like this idea less than making `has_method()` and `get_method_list()` virtual. :-/ This feels kinda hacky and only addresses `JavaClassWrapper`, but none of the other places (ex `JavaScriptBridge`) that also have dynamic methods\r\n\r\nIf we need a short-term solution, I think that should probably be adding `JavaClass::has_java_method()`. Then we can continue discussing a core change for the longer-term?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940162550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940180464","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#issuecomment-2940180464","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107075","id":2940180464,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vP5fw","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T14:06:57Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T14:06:57Z","body":"> > This would introduce a path for `Object` subclasses to define methods that are not registered in `ClassDB`, introducing 'dynamic typing' as a whole new concept to our ecosystem.\r\n> \r\n> It's already possible for classes to have \"dynamic methods\" that aren't registered in `ClassDB`, which is used in a couple places, including `JavaClassWrapper` (for Android) and `JavaScriptBridge` (for the web).\r\n> \r\n> However, those methods aren't currently recognized by `has_method()` and `get_method_list()`\r\n\r\nThat's unfortunate. Do you know the reason for this (i.e. why it's not going through the usual scripting interfaces)?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940180464/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940202806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#issuecomment-2940202806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107075","id":2940202806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vP-82","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek"